# Web Lesson 39 -- finite subobject classification.
# visual: svg
# loops: 0
# ***************************************************************************
# * PREREQUISITES -- finite sets, monomorphisms, pullbacks, and terminal object.
# * CATEGORICAL SETTING -- subsets of the two-point set in finite Set.
# * LAW / UNIVERSAL PROPERTY -- truth pullback classifies the chosen subobject.
# * BOUNDARY -- membership/partiality are encoded, not statically typed.
# * WHAT THIS SHOWS
# * Four membership rows, one characteristic map, and one restricted partial map.
# ***************************************************************************
;
include "lib/finite_subobjects.mlpl"  # reuse finite classification predicates and visual
membership_rows = [[0, 0], [1, 0], [0, 1], [1, 1]]  # all subobjects of X
complete_inventory = u:two_point_subobject_inventory_is_complete(membership_rows)  # CT074
classified_subobject = u:characteristic_map_classifies_subobject([1, 0], [1, 0])  # CT075-CT076
wrong_characteristic_map = 1 - u:characteristic_map_classifies_subobject([1, 0], [0, 1])  # COUNTEREXAMPLE
partial_map_is_well_formed = u:bounded_partial_map_is_well_formed([1, 0], [9])  # CT077
extra_output_rejected = 1 - u:bounded_partial_map_is_well_formed([1, 0], [9, 8])  # COUNTEREXAMPLE
disp(membership_rows)
disp([complete_inventory, classified_subobject, wrong_characteristic_map, partial_map_is_well_formed, extra_output_rejected])
# ***************************************************************************
# * THE VISUAL
# * Inventory subsets, follow χ into truth, then read the restricted partial map.
# ***************************************************************************
def u:finite_subobjects_web_visual() { "Render finite truth classification and a bounded domain-restricted partial map."; u:finite_subobjects_visual() }  # narrated shared visual entry point
finite_subobjects_visual = u:finite_subobjects_web_visual()  # bind visual constant
finite_subobjects_visual  # display bound visual once
# ***************************************************************************
# * HOW TO READ THE RESULT
# * χ=[1,0] marks exactly {0}; the wrong χ marks {1}; output 9 exists only on {0}.
# * THE POINT -- characteristic maps turn subobject membership into an arrow to truth.
# ***************************************************************************
